import Foundation

/// What a Mastodon says on its lines beyond posts and notices, and of what is unread, of its held-back
/// requests and of the three newer kinds of notice (#424), **as a real server sent it**: the Mastodon
/// 4.6.6 images `servers/compose.yml` pins, with worker and streaming up, asked on 2026-11-02 with the
/// seed's writer (`fediqo`). No token is in here.
///
/// ## What was asked, and what the server answered
///
/// | Asked | Mastodon 4.6.6 |
/// | ----- | -------------- |
/// | somebody writes to the writer alone, on `/streaming/user` | `update` where they are followed, and `notification` `mention`; **never `conversation`** |
/// | the same, on `/streaming/direct` | `event: conversation`, the whole conversation |
/// | an announcement published, changed, reacted to, taken down, on `/streaming/user` | `announcement`, `announcement`, `announcement.reaction`, `announcement.delete` |
/// | a filter made, changed, removed, on `/streaming/user` and `/streaming/direct` | **nothing**: `filters_changed` has no payload, and the streaming service drops an event without one |
/// | a post that a new filter catches, on `/streaming/user` | `update`, its `filtered` naming that filter by its changed title, at once |
/// | `GET /api/v1/notifications/unread_count` | `{"count":62}`, of the notices above the `notifications` marker; 100 at most unless `limit` says more, 1000 at most |
/// | the same with `exclude_types[]=added_to_collection` / a word it has not | one fewer / the same, no refusal |
/// | `POST /api/v1/markers` `notifications[last_read_id]` of the newest | 200, and the count is 0 |
/// | the same, of a **lower** id | 200: the marker **goes back**, and the count rises |
/// | that `POST` by a sign-in without `write:statuses` | 403 |
/// | `POST /api/v1/notifications/requests/accept` `id[]` of one held and one it has not | 200 `{}`, the one answered and the other ignored |
/// | that, by a sign-in without `write:notifications` | 403 |
/// | `GET /api/v1/notifications/requests/merged`, just after / some seconds after | `{"merged":false}` / `{"merged":true}`, with `notifications_merged` on the line between |
/// | a post the writer quoted changes | notice `quoted_update`: `account` is who changed it, `status` is **the writer's own quoting post** |
/// | the writer put in a collection, the collection renamed | `added_to_collection`, `collection_update`: `account` its owner, `collection` beside it, on both reads. Made with the collections feature on for the making alone |
